# This repo is developed on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) and built on Linux.
#
# Shell scripts must arrive in the image with LF endings. A CRLF entrypoint.sh
# makes the kernel read the shebang as `/bin/sh\r` and the container dies with
# "no such file or directory" naming an interpreter that plainly exists — one
# of the more confusing ways a deploy can fail, and one that only shows up in
# the deployed environment.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same argument, one layer up: these configure or become the image.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
.dockerignore text eol=lf
